WEBVTT

00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:16,560
How can I discern between feeling ill or sick, whether it's from detoxing or it's from a virus

00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:24,420
or an infection or something? Yeah, that's hard because so, understand, so if I'm detoxing,

00:00:25,620 --> 00:00:36,100
I can feel ill. That's typically called a herximer reaction, named after a doctor herximer who

00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:43,940
initially described it a long time ago. I don't know what it was, but it's very common with people

00:00:43,940 --> 00:00:50,100
with gram-negative bacterial infections that are killing that infection, like Lyme disease,

00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:56,740
Lyme disease is a gram-negative bacteria, has gram-negative bacteria or has lipopolysaccharides

00:00:56,740 --> 00:01:02,980
in the cell membrane. That's what makes it a gram-negative bacteria. And when you kill gram-negative

00:01:02,980 --> 00:01:09,300
bacteria quickly, you will liberate a lot of lipopolysaccharides. And they're quite toxic,

00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:15,700
and they can make a person feel quite ill. Lipopolysaccharides can damage the blood barrier very readily

00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:20,260
and can cross the blood barrier and cause a lot of brain inflammation. It can make you feel really

00:01:20,260 --> 00:01:29,700
yucky. That's called a herximer reaction. So when a detoxine, I can also feel ill. So a herximer

00:01:30,180 --> 00:01:36,020
really is not specific to lipopolysaccharides, but it's specific to anything that overwhelms your

00:01:36,020 --> 00:01:47,220
liver. So if I kill bacteria quickly, if I kill cells quickly, let's say with chemotherapy. So one

00:01:47,220 --> 00:01:52,820
of the reasons why I feel so sick with chemotherapy is I'm taking a drug that's poisoned,

00:01:52,820 --> 00:01:58,500
and that's killing all sorts of cells, and it can damage the blood barrier and cause inflammation

00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:06,020
of the brain. But another reason is that it's killing cells pathologically, not through apoptosis,

00:02:06,660 --> 00:02:12,420
but through cell lysis. So at any time you have cell lysis, pathological cell death,

00:02:13,380 --> 00:02:20,180
you will liberate a lot of what are called endotoxins, cell particles, you know, cell membrane

00:02:21,620 --> 00:02:28,020
junk, and you're going to overwhelm your liver. Your liver is like, I can't take anymore,

00:02:28,020 --> 00:02:32,180
I can't take anymore. Go on, go on, go on. And you got all this junk in your blood, all these

00:02:32,180 --> 00:02:39,620
endotoxins in your blood that can make you feel quite ill. Also, if you're sick, you have a virus,

00:02:39,620 --> 00:02:44,180
you have a bacterial infection, you're going to feel ill. So how do I discern whether I

00:02:44,180 --> 00:02:48,500
have a bacterial infection, have a virus, or I have a herximer reaction?

00:02:50,020 --> 00:02:54,820
Sometimes it's difficult because you could get even a fever with a herximer reaction sometimes.

00:02:55,780 --> 00:03:04,180
So typically, if you did a CBC with differential, that's a blood test, complete blood count.

00:03:04,180 --> 00:03:10,420
I mean, it can be quite easy because that will show you if you're dealing with an infection

00:03:10,420 --> 00:03:16,100
or you feel sick for some other reason. So that would be an easy way. So if we had access to

00:03:16,100 --> 00:03:22,260
if you're in my hospital and you came in feeling empty, we'd do a CBC and a complete metabolic

00:03:22,420 --> 00:03:29,140
animal with that CBC. If you showed an elevation of white blood cells over 7, 7.5,

00:03:30,500 --> 00:03:34,660
I'd say you probably have an infection. And then you would look at the differential of this white

00:03:34,660 --> 00:03:40,820
blood cells. And if you had a elevated neutrophil prepared to lymphocyte, I'd say you probably

00:03:40,820 --> 00:03:44,740
have a little bacterial infection. I mean, if you have a very high white blood cell, I'll call it

00:03:44,740 --> 00:03:52,020
let's say it's a 15. And you have an elevated neutrophil count compared to lymphocyte count. I'd

00:03:52,020 --> 00:03:58,820
say maybe even need to consider getting an antibiotic. If you had an elevated white blood cell count,

00:03:59,700 --> 00:04:05,700
like I said before, and an elevated lymphocyte count in a more suppressed neutrophil count,

00:04:05,700 --> 00:04:10,100
I'd say you probably have a virus. You need to go home and drink some chicken soup and take

00:04:10,100 --> 00:04:16,580
care of yourself. Either way, you probably should do that. So that's the easiest way to know

00:04:16,580 --> 00:04:23,380
whether I'm feeling icky because I have an infection or I'm feeling icky because I'm detoxing.

00:04:24,020 --> 00:04:28,340
But most of us don't just run off and get a blood test. It's just not that easy. Well,

00:04:28,340 --> 00:04:33,860
we're not feeling well. So there's other clues. Other people in my house feel the same way.

00:04:34,820 --> 00:04:39,940
Okay, that's a clue because you're not going to all be detoxing the same way.

00:04:41,060 --> 00:04:46,340
You came from a party or you're exposed to a lot of people or you have more under a lot of stress

00:04:46,340 --> 00:04:52,100
or you know, there's other things that would give you clues for that. Obviously, like I said,

00:04:52,100 --> 00:04:58,500
if you have a fever, it's probably greater chance that you have a sickness from detoxing. If you're

00:04:58,500 --> 00:05:03,380
throwing it up, you feel like you've got the flu. I mean, and then the other thing is if it passes

00:05:03,380 --> 00:05:08,100
pretty quickly. So you had it for a couple days and now you're feeling better if probably was a bug

00:05:08,100 --> 00:05:14,180
or something. So those are the things that I would use to help differential diagnosed between those two.

